{{!
    @template tool_vae/carry_notes

    What a declaration says of its carries: one paragraph where it was carried to, one where it comes from; nothing when
    it has no carry.

    Every text comes from the context, already worded by tool_vae\output\carry_notes. The template holds no logic. Every
    value is escaped (double braces): none of them is HTML.

    Classes required for JS:
    * none

    Data attributes required for JS:
    * none

    Context variables required for this template:
    * notes - array of {text}: the sentences

    Example context (json):
    {
        "notes": [
            {"text": "Carried over to record RS6000 on 1 June 2026. This declaration and its attestation stay as they are."}
        ]
    }
}}
{{#notes}}<p class="tool-vae-carry small text-muted">{{text}}</p>{{/notes}}
